{
  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_004 (multimodal, scvi_n200, resnet50, concat) achieved 0.5362 acc, showing that adding image information to the best RNA encoder (scvi_n200, confirmed by config_008 > config_002) provides a modest ~1.6% gain over RNA-only. However, we have only tested one image encoder (resnet50). Uncertainty: whether a stronger pretrained image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) yields meaningfully better image representations than resnet50, which would affect all downstream multimodal configurations. This experiment (config_009) isolates the image encoder effect by keeping RNA encoder (scvi_n200), profile setting (singleprofile), and fusion (concat) identical to config_004, changing only resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l. This is the best use of the next budget slot because it resolves a fundamental representation question that will inform whether to invest in ViT-based or CNN-based image encoders across many future multiprofile/aggregation experiments, and it is a clean single-variable comparison against an already-completed configuration."
}

